hes, structural samples, and serializable dispersion values\\n\\...\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0033\\\\.spec-md\"}\nThe existing `.spec-md` is empty; now I can write it.\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0033\\\\.spec-md\", \"content\": \"# Spec 0033 — Materials & Library workbenches, structural samples, and serializable dispersion values\\n\\...\nNow the `.spec-jsonl`. First the mandatory read of the (empty) file:\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0033\\\\.spec-jsonl\"}\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0033\\\\.spec-jsonl\", \"content\": \"{\\\"number\\\":1,\\\"anchor\\\":\\\"IMPLEMENT\\\",\\\"ac\\\":\\\"AC-A1\\\",\\\"touches\\\":[\\\"OpticalConstructor.Domain\\\",\\\"...\nBoth files written. Now let me mechanically validate the `.spec-jsonl` against the §9 authoring rules before appending history:\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd \\\"C:/GitHub/Berreman\\\" && python - <<'EOF'\\nimport json, re\\npath = r\\\"specs/0033/.spec-jsonl\\\"\\nANCHORS = {\\\"ADD_CONTRACT\\\",\\\"MODIFY_CONTRACT\\\",\\\"IMPLEMENT_CONT...\nAll §9 checks pass. Now append the history row via the project's safe writer:\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\claude-agent.XDUO.000\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\spec0033-history-payload.txt\", \"content\": \"Authored the full spec 0033 from the preliminary spec C:/GitHub...\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd \\\"C:/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator\\\" && PYTHONPATH=\\\"C:/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator/src\\\" python -m ai_strategy_generator.spec_writer.history_cli append --spec-f...\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd \\\"C:/GitHub/Berreman\\\" && python -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nrows=[json.loads(l) for l in open(r'specs/0033/.history',encoding='utf-8') if l.strip()]\\nprint(len(rows),'r...\nThe full spec for bundle 0033 is authored and committed to the spec folder. Summary of what was produced:\n\n**`specs/0033/.spec-md`** (steering narrative) — binding constraints (engine `…WithDisp` types stay unchanged/non-serializable; elevate-every-primitive; all catalogue IO stays mocked in-memory; forbidden expansions incl. no segment validation and no free 3×3 gyration editor; the Materials/Library/Selector naming; condensed destructive-action UX checklist), the six-contract table, and per-part orientation with recorded decisions. Every `file:line` pointer was Read-verified against the tree before being cited.\n\n**`specs/0033/.spec-jsonl`** — 26 linear steps, validated against the step-compiler's §9 rules (line-number invariant, anchors, forward-only closure, lifecycle completeness, registered prefixes, `WIRE_UI` final step — all pass):\n\n- **Part A (CRITICAL, steps 1–6):** `SampleStructure`/`PeriodGroup` replace `sampleToSystem`'s string-id branching and the silent glass fallback; `MaterialId`/`SampleId` elevate to Guid-backed DUs; `<STORE:MaterialProxy>`/`<STORE:SampleProxy>` contracts with stateful `createInMemory` and the `MaterialStillReferenced` hard-block.\n- **Part B (7–13):** the serializable `…Value` types in the engine (formula primitives, descriptive `ConstantEpsValue`, `EpsAxisDispersion`, three segment flavors, `Eps/Mu/RhoWithDispValue`), symmetry-class gyration with new 222/monoclinic/triclinic builders in `Active.fs`, `DispersionModels` lowering plus Forouhi–Bloomer/Brendel–Bormann/`SumOfTerms`, and `MaterialComplexity`.\n- **Parts C–G (14–25):** Selector rename, domain-free `MaterialsControls`/`SampleLibraryControls`, chart real-move to Controls + second Y axis + n-left/k-right view, `CrystalOrientation`, the pure Domain `SampleStackEditor`, both editor windows, host bay wiring, and RII import formulas 2–7 (8/9 → typed error).\n- **Step 26:** `WIRE_UI` at the App composition root.\n\nThree deviations from the preliminary spec were forced by verified code facts and are recorded as decisions: bulk ops live in a new Domain `SampleStackEditor` (the existing `StackEditor` edits a resolved `OpticalSystem` with no material ids to select by); the editor windows land in `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows` (the Main-screen host references only Domain + Controls, not Ui); and `silicon`/`langasite` stay view-only since their dispersion is coded in engine presets, not expressible as data.\n\n**`specs/0033/.history`** — one `spec`/`output` row appended via the `history_cli` safe writer using the cycle's pinned timestamp and commit ref.\nThe full spec for bundle 0033 is authored and committed to the spec folder. Summary of what was produced:\n\n**`specs/0033/.spec-md`** (steering narrative) — binding constraints (engine `…WithDisp` types stay unchanged/non-serializable; elevate-every-primitive; all catalogue IO stays mocked in-memory; forbidden expansions incl. no segment validation and no free 3×3 gyration editor; the Materials/Library/Selector naming; condensed destructive-action UX checklist), the six-contract table, and per-part orientation with recorded decisions. Every `file:line` pointer was Read-verified against the tree before being cited.\n\n**`specs/0033/.spec-jsonl`** — 26 linear steps, validated against the step-compiler's §9 rules (line-number invariant, anchors, forward-only closure, lifecycle completeness, registered prefixes, `WIRE_UI` final step — all pass):\n\n- **Part A (CRITICAL, steps 1–6):** `SampleStructure`/`PeriodGroup` replace `sampleToSystem`'s string-id branching and the silent glass fallback; `MaterialId`/`SampleId` elevate to Guid-backed DUs; `<STORE:MaterialProxy>`/`<STORE:SampleProxy>` contracts with stateful `createInMemory` and the `MaterialStillReferenced` hard-block.\n- **Part B (7–13):** the serializable `…Value` types in the engine (formula primitives, descriptive `ConstantEpsValue`, `EpsAxisDispersion`, three segment flavors, `Eps/Mu/RhoWithDispValue`), symmetry-class gyration with new 222/monoclinic/triclinic builders in `Active.fs`, `DispersionModels` lowering plus Forouhi–Bloomer/Brendel–Bormann/`SumOfTerms`, and `MaterialComplexity`.\n- **Parts C–G (14–25):** Selector rename, domain-free `MaterialsControls`/`SampleLibraryControls`, chart real-move to Controls + second Y axis + n-left/k-right view, `CrystalOrientation`, the pure Domain `SampleStackEditor`, both editor windows, host bay wiring, and RII import formulas 2–7 (8/9 → typed error).\n- **Step 26:** `WIRE_UI` at the App composition root.\n\nThree deviations from the preliminary spec were forced by verified code facts and are recorded as decisions: bulk ops live in a new Domain `SampleStackEditor` (the existing `StackEditor` edits a resolved `OpticalSystem` with no material ids to select by); the editor windows land in `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows` (the Main-screen host references only Domain + Controls, not Ui); and `silicon`/`langasite` stay view-only since their dispersion is coded in engine presets, not expressible as data.\n\n**`specs/0033/.history`** — one `spec`/`output` row appended via the `history_cli` safe writer using the cycle's pinned timestamp and commit ref."}
